 CODE 
2.3.24. 
Other own debts 
The following are own debts 
1¡ debts contracted by one of the spouses in the exclusive interest of his or her own patrimony; 
2¡ debts resulting from a personal or real security given by one of the spouses in an interest other than that of the common patrimony; 
3¡ debts arising from the exercise by one of the spouses of a profession prohibited to him or her under Article 216 of the former Civil Code or from acts which one of the spouses could not perform without the assistance of his or her spouse or the authorisation of the court; 
4¡ debts arising from a criminal conviction or from an offence or quasi-offence committed by one of the spouses.
